WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.270
Meet Otto.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.470
Otto puts your image requests through to a provider.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.770
This one must use the fox from your approved sketch.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.950
The line that takes sketches is dark.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.690
So Otto drops the must, and plugs in anyway.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.610
Imagen Provider never drops a must, whatever line is lit.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.870
If no lit line can meet it, the call stops and says what to set up.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.050
A preference can bend, with a note saying why.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.810
One interface for agents, terminals and code.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.930
You get the file, and which provider made it.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.840
Its tests made no paid calls.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.990
Real images cost money, and judging the fox stays your job.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.140
Imagen Provider.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.470
Generate the image without losing the requirements.
